Summary:
Today’s internship work focused on understanding and organizing the project foundation for the Developer Portfolio Evaluator. I carefully analyzed the overall project structure to identify the required components and flow. Based on this analysis, I created a clean and logical folder structure to support scalable development. The initial setup was then successfully pushed and updated on GitHub to maintain version control and track progress.
Outcomes:
By completing today’s tasks, I gained a clearer understanding of how to plan and structure a project before development begins. I was able to design a well-organized folder hierarchy that will make future coding and maintenance easier. This activity also improved my practical knowledge of using GitHub for project management and updates. Overall, it established a strong base for continuing the development of the portfolio evaluator efficiently.
